<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>For each statement, decide whether it is an identity (true for every angle <m>x</m> for which both sides are defined) or not an identity.</p><div><m>{\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1}</m> [ identity | not an identity ] </div><div><m>{\sin x - \cos x = 1}</m> [ identity | not an identity ] </div><div><m>{\cos^2 x - \sin^2 x = 1 - 2\sin^2 x}</m> [ identity | not an identity ] </div><div><m>{\sin^2 x - \cos^2 x = 1}</m> [ identity | not an identity ] </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>One value of <m>x</m> where the two sides differ is enough to show a statement is not an identity. Algebra with <m>\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1</m> shows a statement is one.</p><ul><li><m>{\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1}</m>: identity. This is the Pythagorean identity itself.</li><li><m>{\sin x - \cos x = 1}</m>: not an identity. At <m>x = 0^\circ</m> the left side is <m>0 - 1 = -1</m>.</li><li><m>{\cos^2 x - \sin^2 x = 1 - 2\sin^2 x}</m>: identity. Replace <m>\cos^2 x</m> by <m>1 - \sin^2 x</m>.</li><li><m>{\sin^2 x - \cos^2 x = 1}</m>: not an identity. At <m>x = 0^\circ</m> the left side is <m>0 - 1 = -1</m>.</li></ul></p></solution>
    <answer><p>identity</p></answer>
    <answer><p>not an identity</p></answer>
    <answer><p>identity</p></answer>
    <answer><p>not an identity</p></answer>
</stack-static>